{"causes": ["The sustained internal fragmentation and succession crises within the Ava Kingdom from the late 15th century weakened its central authority.", "The strategic alliance and military support provided by the Shan state of Mohnyin enabled Sithu Kyawhtin's rebellion against King Narapati III.", "The expansionist policies of the Toungoo Dynasty exerted immense external pressure on the declining Ava Kingdom, creating an environment ripe for internal upheaval."], "effects": ["Sithu Kyawhtin's overthrow of Narapati III in 1551 marked the definitive end of the direct line of Ava kings and ushered in the kingdom's final, brief independent phase.", "The collapse of the Ava Kingdom under Sithu Kyawhtin in 1555 led directly to its absorption into the First Toungoo Empire, unifying Burma under a single dynasty.", "His reign and subsequent defeat solidified the Toungoo Dynasty's control over Upper Burma, enabling Bayinnaung to consolidate a vast empire across Southeast Asia."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "narapati-iii", "sourceName": "Narapati III", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "targetName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "context": "The internal weaknesses and perceived illegitimacy of Narapati III's rule directly caused Sithu Kyawhtin to launch his rebellion in 1545."}, {"sourceSlug": "mohnyin", "sourceName": "Mohnyin", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "targetName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "context": "The Shan state of Mohnyin provided crucial military and political support to Sithu Kyawhtin during his six-year rebellion against Ava (1545–1551)."}, {"sourceSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "sourceName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "narapati-iii", "targetName": "Narapati III", "context": "Sithu Kyawhtin succeeded Narapati III as king of Ava in 1551 after overthrowing him in a rebellion."}, {"sourceSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "sourceName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "ava-kingdom", "targetName": "Ava Kingdom", "context": "Sithu Kyawhtin's entire reign and the collapse of his kingdom occurred within the historical and geographical context of the Ava Kingdom."}, {"sourceSlug": "first-toungoo-empire", "sourceName": "First Toungoo Empire", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "targetName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "context": "The aggressive expansion of the First Toungoo Empire under Bayinnaung directly caused the downfall and end of Sithu Kyawhtin's reign in 1555."}], "places": [{"name": "Ava, Myanmar", "role": "Capital City"}, {"name": "Mohnyin, Myanmar", "role": "Rebellion Support"}, {"name": "Upper Burma, Myanmar", "role": "Territorial Base"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Sithu Kyawhtin", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "sithu-kyawhtin"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3485504", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sithu_Kyawhtin"], "tags": ["Monarchs & Rulers", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Sithu Kyawhtin's brief reign as the last king of Ava marked the definitive end of an independent Upper Burmese kingdom, a polity that had existed for over 200 years. His defeat by Bayinnaung facilitated the complete unification of Burma under the First Toungoo Empire, a pivotal moment in the region's history.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-13T20:22:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43498900767", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Sithu Kyawhtin was the last king of Ava from 1551 to 1555. He came to power by overthrowing King Narapati III in 1551, the culmination of his six-year rebellion (1545–1551) with the support of the Shan state of Mohnyin.", "newValue": "Sithu Kyawhtin, a Shan chieftain and military commander, emerged as the final sovereign of the Ava Kingdom, reigning from 1551 to 1555. His ascent to power culminated a protracted six-year rebellion against King Narapati III, marking the terminal phase of the Kingdom of Ava, which had dominated Upper Burma for over a century. His brief rule is significant not for its stability or achievements, but as the final, desperate gasp of an internally fractured kingdom before its absorption into the ascendant First Toungoo Empire, fundamentally reshaping the political landscape of 16th-century Southeast Asia.

Sithu Kyawhtin initiated his rebellion in 1545, leveraging the internal weaknesses and succession disputes that plagued the Ava throne. With crucial military backing from the powerful Shan state of Mohnyin, he steadily eroded Ava's authority, culminating in the successful overthrow of King Narapati III in 1551. This victory solidified his control over the capital and surrounding territories, officially establishing him as king. However, his reign was immediately challenged by the relentless expansion of Tabinshwehti's Toungoo forces, which had already unified much of Lower Burma and were systematically conquering the Shan states.

The collapse of Sithu Kyawhtin's Ava Kingdom in 1555, following its conquest by Bayinnaung (Tabinshwehti's successor), heralded the end of an independent Upper Burmese polity that traced its origins back to the Pinya Kingdom of the 14th century. This event was a pivotal moment in Burmese history, symbolizing the final consolidation of disparate regional powers under the ambitious Toungoo dynasty. The subsequent integration of Ava into the First Toungoo Empire laid the groundwork for a unified Burmese state that would, for a period, become the largest empire in Southeast Asian history."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-13T20:22:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43498900767", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1495"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "1495"}], "newValue": ["The sustained internal fragmentation and succession crises within the Ava Kingdom from the late 15th century weakened its central authority.", "The strategic alliance and military support provided by the Shan state of Mohnyin enabled Sithu Kyawhtin's rebellion against King Narapati III.", "The expansionist policies of the Toungoo Dynasty exerted immense external pressure on the declining Ava Kingdom, creating an environment ripe for internal upheaval."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-13T20:22:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43498900767", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": ""}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "Medieval"}], "newValue": ["Sithu Kyawhtin's overthrow of Narapati III in 1551 marked the definitive end of the direct line of Ava kings and ushered in the kingdom's final, brief independent phase.", "The collapse of the Ava Kingdom under Sithu Kyawhtin in 1555 led directly to its absorption into the First Toungoo Empire, unifying Burma under a single dynasty.", "His reign and subsequent defeat solidified the Toungoo Dynasty's control over Upper Burma, enabling Bayinnaung to consolidate a vast empire across Southeast Asia."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-13T20:22:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43498900767", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "sourceName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "verb": "RULES", "targetSlug": "field-221", "targetName": "Monarchs & Rulers", "context": "Sithu Kyawhtin: Sovereign authority in monarchs & rulers"}, {"sourceSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "sourceName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "medieval", "targetName": "Medieval Era", "context": "Sithu Kyawhtin was active during the Medieval era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "narapati-iii", "sourceName": "Narapati III", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "targetName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "context": "The internal weaknesses and perceived illegitimacy of Narapati III's rule directly caused Sithu Kyawhtin to launch his rebellion in 1545."}, {"sourceSlug": "mohnyin", "sourceName": "Mohnyin", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "targetName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "context": "The Shan state of Mohnyin provided crucial military and political support to Sithu Kyawhtin during his six-year rebellion against Ava (1545–1551)."}, {"sourceSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "sourceName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "narapati-iii", "targetName": "Narapati III", "context": "Sithu Kyawhtin succeeded Narapati III as king of Ava in 1551 after overthrowing him in a rebellion."}, {"sourceSlug": "sithu-kyawhtin", "sourceName": "Sithu Kyawhtin", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "ava-kingdom", "targetName": "Ava Kingdom", "context": "Sithu Kyawhtin's entire reign and the co